ovie but once upon a  snowman show  just how an object made of ice and snow  became so obsessed with the heat it of  course happens in the trading post  olaf is on the hunt for a nose and while  he later settles on a summer sausage he  first tries on  a stereoscope the stereoscope is full of  pictures of  summer that get his pupils dilating and  excitement building  speaking of those summer pictures disney  being you know disney couldn't resist  adding a piece of some other hit  movies in the short the pictures of  summer olaf seas  show some familiar sunny places that  exist in moana  and tangled did disney just give their  fans confirmation that all three of  these movies happen in the same universe  it  would explain why fans think that  rapunzel and flynn can be seen  entering the castle for elsa's  coronation  the pictures of summer also foreshadowed  just how olaf's future  in summer jazz number would look or more  specifically  where it would take place there were  cards that featured the field of  dandelions he pranced around  in the beach setup he also imagined  himself in and  even the gazebo that gave off major  sound of music vibes  it makes the fact that a snowman who  claimed to know nothing but knew a whole  lot about summer  makes sense there was also a summer  picture that included a specific red  checkered blanket  if you've watched both frozen films you  might find it a tad familiar  that's because it's popped up multiple  times it's in the summer postcard  reappears in olaf's in summer and then  makes a final appearance in the opening  scene of  some things never change in frozen two  what other way is there to bond disney  characters than  sending them into a wolf chase am i  right in the short we get another point  of view on the wolf chase that anna and  kristoff get themselves involved in  it was actually all olaf's fault he was  the one originally being chased after  the wolves caught the scent of his  summer sausage nose  he of course gets 